WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Sometimes, changing the world begins with something very small.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:17.000
In a neighbourhood in Kigali, a group of young people noticed a problem. Their community had areas filled with litter, and few people seemed willing to do anything about it.

3
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Instead of waiting for someone else to act, they decided to start themselves.

4
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:35.000
One Saturday morning, they gathered with gloves, bags, and a simple plan. They cleaned the streets, collected rubbish, and encouraged their neighbours to join them.

5
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:44.000
At first, only a few people helped. But as the morning continued, more residents came outside. Some brought tools. Others brought water and encouraged the volunteers.

6
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:53.000
By the end of the day, the neighbourhood looked different. More importantly, the people felt connected by something they had accomplished together.

7
00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:06.000
The young volunteers learned an important lesson: meaningful change does not always begin with a big idea or a lot of money. Sometimes, it begins with one person taking the first step.

8
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:14.000
And when others follow, one small action can become something much bigger.

9
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:20.000
This is StoryCast, where every story gives us a new way to see the world.

